cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DDC-Audit in your research, please cite the accompanying paper and this software."
title: "DDC-Audit: calibrated auditing of drug discrimination in single-cell perturbation prediction"
abstract: >-
  A CPU-only pre-submission audit tool that asks whether a single-cell
  perturbation model's stored predictions distinguish held-out drugs within the
  same cellular context. It computes the drug-discrimination control (DDC) AUC,
  a drug-clustered bootstrap interval, a within-cell-line permutation null, and a
  construction-calibration check built from counts-space vehicle pseudobulks.
  It is not a prediction model, a clinical tool, a drug-recommendation system, or
  a cross-model leaderboard.
